{"content":[{"c":["JESSE (P",{"c":["erson"],"sourceClass":"lc","t":"span"},")"],"sourceClass":"h1","t":"p"},{"c":["Son of Obed and grandson of Ruth and Boaz (",{"href":"?bref=Ruth.4.17,22","r":"Ruth.4.17,22","rawR":"Ruth.4.17,22","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ruth.4.17,22","value":"Ruth.4.17,22"}],"t":"ref","v":"Ru 4:17, 22"},"). Jesse was a shepherd from Bethlehem. He had eight sons, of whom David was the youngest. He had at least two daughters, Zeruiah and Abigail, who became mothers of famous warriors."],"sourceClass":"fl","t":"p"},{"c":["When Samuel went to Jesse’s home to search for and anoint a king, Jesse did not at first feel it worthwhile to call David for examination (",{"href":"?bref=1Sam.16.11","r":"1Sam.16.11","rawR":"1Sam.16.11","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Sam.16.11","value":"1Sam.16.11"}],"t":"ref","v":"1 Sm 16:11"},"). Later he sent David to play the lyre for Saul (vv ",{"href":"?bref=1Sam.16.19-21","r":"1Sam.16.19-21","rawR":"1Sam.16.19-21","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Sam.16.19-21","value":"1Sam.16.19-21"}],"t":"ref","v":"19-21"},"). After David became a fugitive from Saul, Jesse and others of the family came to David in the cave of Adullam. David then brought his father and mother to Mizpah in Moab (",{"href":"?bref=1Sam.22.3","r":"1Sam.22.3","rawR":"1Sam.22.3","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Sam.22.3","value":"1Sam.22.3"}],"t":"ref","v":"22:3"},"). Nothing further is heard of Jesse."],"sourceClass":"","t":"p"},{"c":["After Saul broke with David, he commonly spoke of David derisively as a “son of Jesse” to underscore his humble origins (",{"href":"?bref=1Sam.20.31","r":"1Sam.20.31","rawR":"1Sam.20.31","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Sam.20.31","value":"1Sam.20.31"}],"t":"ref","v":"1 Sm 20:31"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=1Sam.22.7","r":"1Sam.22.7","rawR":"1Sam.22.7","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Sam.22.7","value":"1Sam.22.7"}],"t":"ref","v":"22:7"},"). This same emphasis on Jesse’s modest station in life is found in such messianic references as ",{"href":"?bref=Isa.11.1","r":"Isa.11.1","rawR":"Isa.11.1","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Isa.11.1","value":"Isa.11.1"}],"t":"ref","v":"Isaiah 11:1"}," and ",{"href":"?bref=Isa.10.1-34","r":"Isa.10.1-34","rawR":"Isa.10.1-34","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Isa.10.1-34","value":"Isa.10.1-34"}],"t":"ref","v":"10"},", which speak of the “shoot from the stump of Jesse” and “the root of Jesse” (",{"c":["rsv"],"sourceClass":"sc","t":"span"},")."],"sourceClass":"","t":"p"},{"c":[{"c":["See also"],"sourceClass":"ital","t":"span"}," ",{"href":"?item=David_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","id":"David_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","rawId":"David_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","t":"link","v":"David"},"; ",{"href":"?item=JesseRootof_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","id":"JesseRootof_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","rawId":"JesseRootof_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","t":"link","v":"Jesse, Root of"},"."],"sourceClass":"","t":"p"}],"format":"bsb-study-dictionary-v2","id":"JessePerson","provenance":{"archiveSha256":"10758ea00dbea7540f9337e43e59c8e4000295c1261e3426bab6f31c31dcff5b","release":"1.6","sourceCitationReferences":[{"anchorText":"Ru 4:17, 22","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Ruth.4.17,22","rawQueryValue":"Ruth.4.17,22","sourceRefExact":"Ruth.4.17,22"},{"anchorText":"1 Sm 16:11","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=1Sam.16.11","rawQueryValue":"1Sam.16.11","sourceRefExact":"1Sam.16.11"},{"anchorText":"19-21","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=1Sam.16.19-21","rawQueryValue":"1Sam.16.19-21","sourceRefExact":"1Sam.16.19-21"},{"anchorText":"22:3","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=1Sam.22.3","rawQueryValue":"1Sam.22.3","sourceRefExact":"1Sam.22.3"},{"anchorText":"1 Sm 20:31","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=1Sam.20.31","rawQueryValue":"1Sam.20.31","sourceRefExact":"1Sam.20.31"},{"anchorText":"22:7","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=1Sam.22.7","rawQueryValue":"1Sam.22.7","sourceRefExact":"1Sam.22.7"},{"anchorText":"Isaiah 11:1","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Isa.11.1","rawQueryValue":"Isa.11.1","sourceRefExact":"Isa.11.1"},{"anchorText":"10","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Isa.10.1-34","rawQueryValue":"Isa.10.1-34","sourceRefExact":"Isa.10.1-34"}],"sourceItemFragmentSha256":"19d181b2716e3f1e53622d5d624f719a5c53b31c05725c1691f0f78fafc569c0","sourceItemName":"JessePerson","sourceItemOrder":220,"sourceMember":"Articles/J.xml","supplementPointersNotIncludedAsContent":[]},"sourceAttributes":{"name":"JessePerson","product":"TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","typename":"Article"},"sourceTitleExact":"Jesse (Person)","title":"Jesse (Person)","version":"v2-a101d843a2f0cd3fc0c6"}